# Supabase target: Migration branch only

Until the user explicitly says otherwise, every database migration, SQL apply, and Edge Function deploy goes to the **Migration** preview branch — not production, not staging.

| | |
|---|---|
| Branch name | `Migration` |
| Project ref | `supmsgcubipmmowrzoub` |
| API URL | `https://supmsgcubipmmowrzoub.supabase.co` |
| Parent (do not touch) | production `sxkpcovbyaficvtkpsdo` |
| Staging (do not touch) | `axdcledcyhyvzrnfkwat` |

## Must

- Pass `project_id: "supmsgcubipmmowrzoub"` to MCP `apply_migration`, `execute_sql`, `deploy_edge_function`, and related tools.
- Use `supabase ... --project-ref supmsgcubipmmowrzoub` for CLI.
- Keep local `.env` / `worker/.env` pointed at this ref.

## Must not

- Do not apply migrations or deploy functions to `sxkpcovbyaficvtkpsdo` (production) or `axdcledcyhyvzrnfkwat` (staging).
- Do not call `merge_branch` on Migration unless the user explicitly asks to promote it.
- Do not relink the CLI back to production without asking.
